[02:07.72] Desert shadows creep across purple sands.
[02:08.92] Natives kneel in prayer by their caravans.
[02:08.92] There, silhouetted under and eastern star,
[02:08.98] I see my long lost blossom of shalimar
[02:08.98] You, Misirlou, Are the moon and the sun, fairest one.
[02:09.24] Old temple bells are calling across the sand.
[02:09.24] We'll find our Kismet, answering love's command.
[02:09.68] You, Misirlou, are a dream of delight in the night.
[02:10.40] To an oasis, sprinkled by stars above,
[02:10.44] Heaven will guide us, Allah will bless our love.
